WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.120
Wub-a-lub-a-dub-dub Wisecrack, Jared here.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.250
You've probably noticed the internet has blown
up talking about the season 3 premiere of

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.370
Rick and Morty: The Rickshank Redemption.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:18.320
But rather than focusing on the fact that
Justin Roiland and Dan Harmon pulled off quite

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.360
possibly the greatest anti-April Fool's prank
of all time, everyone can't stop talking about

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.370
that sweet Szechuan dipping sauce.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.540
Is the show doing something more profound
than invoking a totally random promotional

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.060
condiment from the Clinton era?

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.020
Absolutely.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.030
And we’re here to break it down for you.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.370
Welcome to this Wisecrack Edition on the Philosophy
of Szechuan Sauce.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:44.070
We’ve talked about the existential themes
in Rick and Morty before.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.780
Between Rick's creations despairing over their
existence

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.520
a persistent resentment towards one's creators

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.120
and Morty's unique life philosophy

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.400
they’re not exactly hiding it.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.440
The show has also dabbled in a sort of relative
to existentialism known as “Absurdism.”

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:17.020
According to French philosopher Albert Camus,
we live a cruel and absurd existence.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:22.310
Humans are cursed with seeking meaning in a universe
that will remain forever silent, and the image

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:27.130
of a guy pushing a boulder up a mountain for
all eternity is the perfect metaphor for the

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.270
human condition.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:32.190
In the spirit of Camus, Rick and Morty paints
an absurd, meaningless multi-verse.

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:36.360
Rick, accordingly, has a long history of trivializing
everything.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.600
He doesn't believe in things like love

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:45.440
or
tradition.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:52.980
Rick's companionship with Morty is, allegedly,
only a means for Rick to hide his genius brain

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.150
waves from the government.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:59.220
In the Rickshank Redemption, we see similar
themes: the arbitrary nature of our social systems,

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.180
mocking sentimentality

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.660
and the pointlessness
of it all.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:18.460
That we live in a meaningless world is an
idea held by both absurdism and existentialism,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:23.180
but the transition from the end of season
2 to the premiere of season 3 really solidifies

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.140
Rick and Morty as an "absurd" work.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.300
It does so by dangling meaning and hope in
front of us, only to rip it to shreds

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.819
Something notable happens at the end of season
2.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:40.100
Rick takes a break from his sociopathic shenanigans
to have an authentic, heartfelt moment at

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.160
Birdperson's wedding.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:56.060
But the show undercuts it when we learn that Tammy
is a spy.

00:02:56.069 --> 00:03:00.689
What makes this part special is that Rick's
flirtation with being a normal, caring, person

00:03:00.689 --> 00:03:04.840
is undercut by an outside force, not his own
cynicism.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.390
This is further explored at the end of the
episode.

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:11.169
After the family is forced into hiding from
the Galactic Federation, Rick overhears the

00:03:11.169 --> 00:03:13.150
hardships he has created for them.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:16.980
In a moment of seeming anguish, Rick turns
himself over to the federation,

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:26.060
and will likely spend the rest of his days in prison.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:30.520
In sacrificing himself, The finale suggests
Rick is wrestling with something he's never

00:03:30.529 --> 00:03:33.060
dealt with: living with meaning.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:37.969
Given complete knowledge of the meaninglessness
of love, life, etc, he chose to do right by

00:03:37.969 --> 00:03:39.769
his family regardless.

00:03:39.769 --> 00:03:44.139
The cliffhanger teases a possible shift in
the show’s existential themes.

00:03:44.139 --> 00:03:49.809
This idea, of creating meaning in a meaningless
world, is one championed by many existentialists,

00:03:49.809 --> 00:03:52.089
but firmly rejected by Camus.

00:03:52.089 --> 00:03:56.919
This crossroads for the show parallels a beef
Camus had with a particular thinker, one who

00:03:56.919 --> 00:04:01.739
regularly contributes to my angst boners - Fyodor
Dostoevsky.

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:06.659
Camus writes that authors, like Dostoevsky,
often propose absurd worlds with characters

00:04:06.659 --> 00:04:11.689
who understand the frivolity of life, only
to chicken out and retreat to the comfort

00:04:11.689 --> 00:04:14.840
of meaning- like religion n' shit.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.590
Dostoevsky's problem, for Camus, is that he
offers a reply to the absurd - some form of

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:24.530
meaning - whereas "an absurd work, on the
contrary, does not provide a reply."

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:29.800
Existentialists like Jean-Paul Sartre or Dostoevsky
may realize the absurdity of existence, but

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:34.790
their analysis fails by resorting to hope,
or trying to create meaning.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:40.139
Camus said of them: "they deify what crushes
them and find reason to hope in what impoverishes

00:04:40.139 --> 00:04:41.139
them."

00:04:41.139 --> 00:04:44.860
At the end of season 2, we may have thought
the the show would make a similar retreat

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:49.031
into meaning and sentimentality, but with
the release of The Rickshank Redemption, we

00:04:49.031 --> 00:04:51.440
now know this is not the case.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:54.150
Instead, it doubles down on the absurd.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.620
Not only was Rick's imprisonment a ploy

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.580
but
the show replies to our prospect of a humanized

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.360
Rick with a journey that will be darker than
ever.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:18.091
And if just to fuck with us even more, much of Rickshanks's comedy is not derived

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:23.069
from joking about life's meaningless like
previous episodes, but rather, the jokes are

00:05:23.069 --> 00:05:25.940
largely derived from our ATTEMPT to draw meaning.

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:34.980
For example, when Rick explores the memory
of him creating the portal gun, we learn that

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:39.870
Beth and Diane were brutally murdered - turning
Rick from a family man to a deranged loner

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:45.560
scientist - your typical tragic Walter White-style
anti-hero origin story that would give meaning

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:46.919
to his madness.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:52.040
This baits the audience to empathize with
Rick - But the joke's on you- it's all a ruse.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.490
So it's not just that Rick and Morty evades
meaning.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:04.370
The writers seem to get a perverse joy in playing
with our desire to search for hope and meaning,

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:08.249
as if Camus was making his point in the style
of an internet troll.

00:06:08.249 --> 00:06:13.289
In another instance, Rick saves Earth from
the Brave New World-inspired Galactic Federation.

00:06:13.289 --> 00:06:19.439
We may be tempted to say that Rick for a greater
good- to liberate earth from their alien oppressors.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:24.080
However Summer's comment suggests that the
new world order doesn't sound too good either.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:34.680
In other moments, the idea that Rick cares
about Morty and Summer is also toyed with.

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:40.660
First, Rick seems to care, as he rushes to
rescue Morty and Summer after learning they’re

00:06:40.669 --> 00:06:42.169
imprisoned by the council of Ricks.

00:06:42.169 --> 00:06:46.840
Rick then exhibits a casual disregard for
Summer’s life in his stand-off with another Rick,

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.000
but we learn it was all part of a well-crafted
strategy.

00:06:55.009 --> 00:07:00.419
Finally, the whole Rick-caring-theory disintegrates agai
as he explains he only saved them so that

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:02.020
Beth doesn’t kick him out of the house.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:09.780
Which finally brings us to the Szechaun Sauce.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:16.020
Rick isn’t motivated by family, or justice,
or love, but only that Mulan mcnugget sauce.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:20.319
The show, undercutting even the most promising
attempt to give Rick a sense of morality,

00:07:20.319 --> 00:07:24.509
doubles-down by suggesting that his entire
series arc will be his quest for a forgotten

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:25.640
promotional food item.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:38.120
But is this really what drives Rick?

00:07:38.129 --> 00:07:39.129
No.

00:07:39.129 --> 00:07:42.669
The only thing Rick's love of Szechuan sauce
means, is that it means nothing.

00:07:42.669 --> 00:07:47.009
The quest for Szechuan sauce isn’t creating
meaning, it’s a reflection of the absurdity

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:49.499
of being driven by, well, anything.

00:07:49.499 --> 00:07:53.949
Given the utter void of meaning in the world,
why not dedicate yourself to an absurd quest

00:07:53.949 --> 00:07:56.120
for plum-flavored McNugget sauce?

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:59.400
Why not spend 9 whole seasons doing it?

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:00.400
Why not 97 years?

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:07.379
The quest for mcnugget sauce is meaningful
only in that its a joke about meaninglessness.

00:08:07.379 --> 00:08:12.090
Camus say that any figure who understands
and finds happiness in the pointless of it

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.259
all is an "Absurd hero."

00:08:14.259 --> 00:08:18.509
The absurd hero must not only be happy with
life’s absurdity, but fully comprehend the

00:08:18.509 --> 00:08:23.020
cosmic indifference that surrounds him - he
calls it “lucid indifference.”

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.740
And this all seems a lot like Rick.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:31.370
A man who's knowledge of the vast multiverse,
where everything terrible and good can and

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.780
has happened, defines his existence.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:39.620
A man who reduces our basic morals to genetic
programming.

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:44.790
A man who, in spite of being able to accomplish
anything, only yearns for Szechuan sauce.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:50.160
There’s also one important difference between
Camus’ absurd hero and Rick Sanchez: absurd

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.250
heroes find happiness in the absurd.

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:55.240
But as we know, Rick is in great pain.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:06.370
Maybe Rick’s actual arc will not be to give
more shits, or be nicer to his family, but

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.660
actually to enjoy the absurdity of it all.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:13.000
So is the April fools joke the fact that they
actually dropped the episode exactly when

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:13.920
they said they would?

00:09:17.640 --> 00:09:23.200
Or is the real joke the prospect of Rick finding
meaning- aka the Szechuanuahn sauce.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:28.649
Essentially- if you thought Rick's self sacrifice
was an indication of a belief in family, justice,

00:09:28.649 --> 00:09:29.920
or anything, for that matter.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.400
You've been had.

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:41.060
Wub-a-lub-a-dub-dub Wisecrack. And to check out our other Rick and Morty videos, click the links here.

